# Redoubt isolation-media-prefs.patch  (Android, android.txt, 158.0-2)
# Owner: LW-M7-50; docs/android/ISOLATION-MEDIA.md section 2a
#
# Owner decision 2026-10-11, verbatim: "158.0-2, Android 12+ only".
#
# Upstream files touched
# ----------------------
#   mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/GeckoRuntime.java
#   mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/process/GeckoProcessManager.java
#   modules/libpref/Preferences.cpp
#
# The media configuration follows the process model, by construction:
#
# 1. GeckoProcessManager.isContentIsolated() is true when the content process
#    type the allocator picks (GeckoProcessType.determineContentProcessType(),
#    the very function that chooses between tab / isolatedTab / zygoteTab) is
#    not plain CONTENT.
# 2. GeckoRuntime.init(), right after it configured the process manager from
#    GeckoRuntimeSettings (isolatedProcessEnabled / appZygoteProcessEnabled,
#    set by Fenix's GeckoProvider from the SDK level, isolation-media-process.patch),
#    adds media.redoubt-isolation-media.enabled = pm.isContentIsolated() to the
#    initial prefs. It does so after the debug config was merged, so a debug
#    config (debuggable apps, or am set-debug-app) cannot override it. The map
#    travels to Gecko as MOZ_DEFAULT_PREFS, the default branch, parsed in
#    Preferences::GetInstanceForService() before the profile's prefs.js and
#    before autoconfig (docs/android/AGENTS.md, landmine L2, stages 2-4).
# 3. Preferences::GetInstanceForService(), in the parent only, immediately after
#    that parse: locks the gate pref at the value GeckoView gave, and only when
#    it is true sets upstream's eleven isolated-process media prefs on the
#    default branch and locks them. Locks win over prefs.js, librewolf.cfg,
#    about:config and GeckoView:SetDefaultPrefs (AGENTS.md L2); child processes
#    receive values and locks from the parent.
#
# So on Android 12+ the eleven are exactly what overlay-isolation-media.cfg
# locked in the prototype (docs/android/expected-prefs-isolation-media.txt),
# and on Android 8-11 not one media pref is touched: each keeps its 158.0-1
# value, unlocked (docs/android/expected-prefs-no-isolation.txt). No pref file
# carries them any more; librewolf.cfg (settings/common.cfg + android.cfg) sets
# none of the twelve names, so nothing fights the gate.
#
# The eleven, name for name and value for value from bug 1988531 part 1,
# mozilla-firefox e0286afb5f6836d607a3f218a527db69979c0bbd (2026-10-06, Firefox
# 159), taskcluster/test_configs/variants.yml, variant geckoview-isolated-process.
# All are `mirror: always` static prefs in 158.0
# (modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml) and nothing under mobile/android
# writes them at runtime.
#
# Re-verify at every rebase: GeckoRuntime.init() still configures the process
# manager before building GeckoThread.InitInfo; determineContentProcessType()
# is still the allocator's only choice of content type; MOZ_DEFAULT_PREFS is
# still parsed in GetInstanceForService(); variants.yml still lists the eleven.
#
